Same-race sacrifice will convert the alter to chaotic if it's lawful or
neutral. If it's already chaotic, it summons a major Demon ('&'), which is
peaceful if you're chaotic, and hostile otherwise.  If you're not chaotic,
then you lose 5 alignment & luck, and increase your god's anger by 3 (AND
have the above mentioned hostile major demon, and you're "terrified, and
unable to move").  If you are chaotic, you gain 2 luck & 5 alignment.  I'm
fairly certain those are the only things that happen on same-race
sacrifice; even for chaotics it will NOT mollify an angry god in the least
(but at least it won't increase the anger), and you will NOT gain any
gifts from same-race sacrifice.


